From 0a9db8a268c816ace1a34bc6e3f5ee1dbf298493 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dotheroes <dotheroes@localhost>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:07:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 16/28] SPU: relocatable overlays (spu_lifter --relocatable)

FMOD Ex's SPU mixer DMAs its codec and DSP plugins (position-independent
SPU ELFs linked at LS 0x80) into its local store wherever it has room and
branches in; 3D Dot Game Heroes' first codec lands at LS 0x156F0. Code
lifted at one address could not run there, which left the interpreter as
the only way in.

spu_lifter.py --relocatable lifts at the link address and routes every
PC-derived value -- brsl/bisl links, lqr/stqr addresses, drain return
PCs, SPU_DIRECT targets -- through SPU_RELOC(x) = x + _rl, where _rl is
ctx->ls_reloc captured at function entry and put back after each nested
call. Absolute branches in such code stop with spu_unsupported.

spu_overlay_register_relocatable(content_ea, link_lsa, span, image, code)
registers one: a GET from content_ea into any LS address makes it
resident with delta = lsa - link_lsa, the first dispatch verifies the
code bytes at the displaced address, lookups translate lsa - delta, and
spu_lifted_lookup publishes the delta in ctx->ls_reloc. A context that
never loads one keeps ls_reloc 0, so such a lift also runs at its link
address unchanged.

build_spu_workloads.py --relocatable IMAGE=EA wires both up.
SPU_OVL_TRACE=<lo>-<hi> logs GETs from a source EA range.
